{"type":"standard","title":"Greg Abbott","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Greg Abbott</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q5605224","titles":{"canonical":"Greg_Abbott","normalized":"Greg Abbott","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Greg Abbott</span></span>"},"pageid":1492735,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Greg_Abbott_2015.jpg/330px-Greg_Abbott_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":458},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b3/Greg_Abbott_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2054,"height":2848},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1379968537","tid":"5e085d4c-c69c-11f1-b1da-f4b959cbf2b4","timestamp":"2026-10-13T00:23:52Z","description":"Governor of Texas since 2015","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greg_Abbott","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greg_Abbott?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greg_Abbott?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Greg_Abbott"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greg_Abbott","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Greg_Abbott","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greg_Abbott?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Greg_Abbott"}},"extract":"Gregory Wayne Abbott is an American politician, attorney, and jurist serving since 2015 as the 48th governor of Texas. A member of the Republican Party, he served from 2002 to 2015 as the 50th attorney general of Texas and from 1996 to 2001 as a justice of the Texas Supreme Court. As of 2025, Abbott is the longest-serving incumbent governor in the United States.","extract_html":"<p><b>Gregory Wayne Abbott</b> is an American politician, attorney, and jurist serving since 2015 as the 48th governor of Texas. A member of the Republican Party, he served from 2002 to 2015 as the 50th attorney general of Texas and from 1996 to 2001 as a justice of the Texas Supreme Court. As of 2025, Abbott is the longest-serving incumbent governor in the United States.</p>"}